@startuml
title UC01 - Hybrid activation and recovery (REVIEW)
autonumber
actor "CSKH application" as C
participant "Access policy" as Auth
participant "Activation service" as A
participant "Request outcomes" as R
participant "Verified customer profiles" as P
participant "Number inventory" as N
participant "Subscriber / MAIN" as S
C -> Auth : JWT + activation/evidence authority
Auth --> C : permitted caller or reject
C -> A : requestId, profile, mode, selectedNumber, consent
A -> R : resolve caller + UC01 + ID / canonical content
alt same key, different content
 R --> A : IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT
 A --> C : conflict, no business effect
else same key, same content exists
 R --> A : current / saved outcome
 A --> C : replay / PROCESSING / WAITING / tombstone
else new request
 A -> P : verify evidence reference and compare every supplied field
 alt invalid evidence / mismatched linked profile
  P --> A : reject; never merge by name and birthdate
  A -> R : terminal FAILED
  A --> C : business failure
 else valid customer
  A -> N : selected availability or random available number
  alt number available, allocation wins
   group one consistent completion
    A -> N : assign number at most once
    A -> S : create Subscriber + MAIN balance0
    A -> R : record SUCCEEDED
   end
   A --> C : final SUCCEEDED after commit
  else selected number unavailable
   A -> R : record FAILED, no automatic substitution
   A --> C : selected number conflict, never WAITING
  else automatic inventory empty
   alt explicit wait consent
    A -> R : WAITING + original deadline<=24h
    A --> C : WAITING (not success)
   else no wait consent
    A -> R : FAILED NO_AVAILABLE_NUMBER
    A --> C : final failure, new attempt needs new ID
   end
  end
 end
end
... number inventory replenished OR recovery every60s ...
participant "Activation recovery" as W
W -> R : eligible WAITING FIFO, original deadlines
loop waiting requests in business priority
 W -> N : allocate if available, recheck conditions
 alt completed before deadline
  W -> S : create exactly one Subscriber + MAIN
  W -> R : SUCCEEDED, consistent completion
 else deadline reached
  W -> R : EXPIRED, no allocation after deadline
 else no number
  W -> R : retain WAITING, same deadline
 end
end
C -> A : lookup same requestId after timeout / WAITING
A -> R : caller-owned outcome only
R --> A : current outcome
A --> C : outcome; never infer rollback from HTTP timeout
note over R,W
 Stock signals can be lost/duplicated; recovery uses persisted truth.
 Concurrent allocation/expiry/retry yields one terminal outcome.
 Recovery60s is not package renewal cadence.
end note
@enduml
